+++ b/scripts/delivery-routes.tsv
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# PLAN-183 W5 — delivery route table. THIS FILE IS THE TRUTH for its three
+# readers (the manifest generator, the upgrader and doctor); scripts/install.sh's
+# writers still carry their destinations in code, and CI checks that PARITY
+# (D3) instead of deriving it (v1.4.0-rc.1 conditions 8 and 62).
+# Destination relpath -> (source relpath, transformation). Reasoning lives
+# in PLAN-183 §8.5.1/§8.5.2; for the readers above the values live ONLY here.
+# A second copy in bash or Python that DECIDES ownership would be the "local
+# branch" CLAUDE.md §4 forbids; the installer's copies deliver, they do not decide.
+# Writers in scripts/install.sh (re-measured for v1.4.0-rc.1, round 11): the
+# functions install_docs_template, install_docs_templates and
+# install_github_templates; CODEOWNERS is rendered by _render_owner_handle
+# (no sed). Line numbers move — locate the SYMBOLS, not a line. Both
+# delivery functions are gated on CEREMONY != user.
+# Conventions: transform = "identity" (verbatim cp) or "substitute:<token>".
+#   flag_dep = the install.sh flag the route depends on; "-" = unconditional,
+#   "!github-owner" = the else-branch taken when the flag is ABSENT.
+# WARNING: .github/CODEOWNERS and .github/CODEOWNERS.template are MUTUALLY
+#   EXCLUSIVE (install.sh --github-owner takes the CODEOWNERS branch, its absence
+#   the .template branch): one run delivers one of the two, never both — and a
+#   `user` ceremony, a missing source or a preserved destination deliver fewer
+#   than the remaining routes. A table keyed by DESTINATION needs both rows anyway.
+# note carries PROSE ONLY. Structured values live in columns.
+dest	src	transform	flag_dep	origin	note
+docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md	templates/docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md	identity	-	install_docs_templates	D2: a root homonym exists; comparing against it reports UNCLASSIFIED where the truth is STALE
+docs/rotation-log.md	templates/docs/rotation-log.md	identity	-	install_docs_templates	D2: a root homonym exists; latent, same class as BRANCH-PROTECTION.md
+.github/CODEOWNERS	templates/.github/CODEOWNERS.template	substitute:{{OWNER_HANDLE}}	github-owner	install_github_templates	rendered at install by _render_owner_handle in install_github_templates; the delivered bytes exist nowhere in a checkout, so it resolves to None fail-LOUD
+.github/CODEOWNERS.template	templates/.github/CODEOWNERS.template	identity	!github-owner	install_github_templates	else-branch: same source as the rendered row, different destination
+.github/workflows/validate.yml.template	templates/.github/workflows/validate.yml.template	identity	-	install_github_templates	the .template suffix SURVIVES delivery; the adopter never gets a live workflow from install
+.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml.template	templates/.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml.template	identity	-	install_github_templates	the .template suffix SURVIVES delivery; the adopter never gets a live workflow from install
