.claude/plans/PLAN-185/s329-ceremony-C/rail-round-2.md:12:- [P1] Preflight fixed project templates before any write — scripts/install.sh:991-996
.claude/plans/PLAN-185/s329-ceremony-C/rail-round-2.md:13:  On a fresh maintainer target with `CLAUDE.md`, `MEMORY.md`, or `.mcp.json` planted as a dangling symlink, this global list passes because those fixed destinations are omitted. Their later `install_template` check records the refusal only after `.claude/`, `docs/`, and `.github/` have been populated; because a fresh target has no `BACKUP_DIR`, the final failure leaves a large unmanifested partial install. Add these known destinations to the global preflight at `scripts/install.sh:991-1005`.
.claude/plans/PLAN-185/s329-ceremony-C/rail-round-2.md:15:- [P1] Reject resolved symlinks used as target roots — scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:766-773
.claude/plans/PLAN-185/s329-ceremony-C/rail-round-2.md:16:  When the caller supplies an existing resolved symlink as the target root, `-e` is true, so this branch never checks `-L`; the subsequent `cd -P` changes the confinement baseline to the referent and accepts every write beneath it. Thus the installer writes through the root symlink instead of issuing the refusal promised by `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:763-765`; test `-L` before resolving the root.
