.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-2.txt:6:Concrete failure: with `delivery-routes.tsv` missing, header-corrupt, or containing a rejected row, install still copies the hard-coded `docs/` and `.github/` destinations. Registration returns success at line 1866, manifest generation returns success at line 1245, install-state is written, and the process reports successful completion with an absent or partial ownership baseline. A caller checking only `$?` cannot distinguish this from a complete install. This contradicts the new classification of the table as required, untrusted input that fails closed.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-2.txt:9:P1 — `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1121`  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-2.txt:10:Concrete failure: the gate claims to require a regular table, but `-f` follows symlinks. A symlinked `scripts/delivery-routes.tsv` is therefore read—and the upgrade snapshot dereferences it—without preserving evidence that its bytes came from outside the checkout. A well-formed external table can reroute an absent `.github/CODEOWNERS` to another allowed `templates/*` source and the upgrade will install those wrong bytes successfully.  
